.TH "REPROCTL\-WORKTREE" "1" "2026" "reproctl" "Repro Development Tools"
.SH NAME
reproctl\-worktree \- manage git worktrees
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]reproctl worktree\f[R] \f[I]subcommand\f[R] [\f[I]options\f[R]]
[\f[I]branch\f[R]]
.PP
\f[B]reproctl wt\f[R] \f[I]subcommand\f[R] [\f[I]options\f[R]]
[\f[I]branch\f[R]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage git worktrees for isolated development.
\f[B]wt\f[R] is a shorthand alias for \f[B]worktree\f[R].
.SS Subcommands
.TP
\f[B]create\f[R] [\f[B]\-\-from\-issue\f[R] \f[I]id\f[R]] [\f[B]\-\-no\-status\-update\f[R]] [\f[B]\-\-skip\-install\f[R]] [\f[B]\-\-dry\-run\f[R]] \f[I]branch\f[R]
Create a new git worktree for \f[I]branch\f[R].
If the branch does not exist, it is created from the current HEAD.
After checkout, runs \f[B]pnpm install\f[R], copies \f[B].env\f[R] files
from the main checkout, and runs \f[B]direnv allow\f[R] in the new
worktree.
With \f[B]\-\-from\-issue\f[R], fetches the branch name from a Linear
issue and sets it to In Progress.
With \f[B]\-\-skip\-install\f[R], dependency installation and package
building are skipped and left to the caller.
.TP
\f[B]remove\f[R] [\f[B]\-\-dry\-run\f[R]] [\f[I]branch\f[R]]
Remove the worktree for \f[I]branch\f[R] via \f[B]git worktree
remove\f[R], then run \f[B]git worktree prune\f[R] to clean up stale
references.
If \f[I]branch\f[R] is omitted and stdin is a terminal, an interactive
picker is shown.
.TP
\f[B]list\f[R]
Show all active worktrees and their associated branches.
.TP
\f[B]attach\f[R] [\f[I]branch\f[R]]
Drop into a new subshell with the working directory set to the worktree
for \f[I]branch\f[R].
Exit the subshell to return to your previous directory.
If \f[I]branch\f[R] is omitted and stdin is a terminal, an interactive
picker is shown.
.TP
\f[B]prune\f[R] [\f[B]\-\-dry\-run\f[R]] [\f[B]\-\-yes\f[R]]
Remove worktrees whose branches have been merged into main or whose
upstream tracking branch no longer exists on the remote.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[B]\-\-dry\-run\f[R]
Preview the operations that would be performed by \f[B]create\f[R],
\f[B]remove\f[R], or \f[B]prune\f[R] without making any changes.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-from\-issue\f[R], \f[B]\-i\f[R] \f[I]id\f[R]
Fetch the branch name from a Linear issue (e.g., \f[B]REP\-123\f[R]).
Only valid with \f[B]create\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]\-\-no\-status\-update\f[R]
Skip setting the Linear issue to In Progress.
Only valid with \f[B]\-\-from\-issue\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]\-\-skip\-install\f[R]
Skip running \f[B]pnpm install\f[R] and \f[B]moon run :build\f[R] after
checkout.
Only valid with \f[B]create\f[R].
Dependency installation is deferred to the caller (for example, the
deliver CLI sends \f[B]pnpm install\f[R] to the workspace terminal
pane).
.TP
\f[B]\-\-yes\f[R], \f[B]\-y\f[R]
Skip the confirmation prompt when pruning.
.SH INTERACTIVE PICKER
When \f[B]attach\f[R] or \f[B]remove\f[R] is called without a branch
name and stdin is a terminal, an interactive picker is shown.
If \f[B]fzf\f[R] is installed, it provides fuzzy selection; otherwise a
numbered prompt is displayed.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
reproctl worktree create feat/my\-feature
Create a worktree, install dependencies, and configure direnv.
.TP
reproctl wt create feat/my\-feature
Same as above using the shorthand alias.
.TP
reproctl wt attach feat/my\-feature
Drop into the worktree subshell.
.TP
reproctl worktree list
Show all active worktrees.
.TP
reproctl worktree remove feat/my\-feature
Remove a worktree and prune references.
.TP
reproctl wt remove \-\-dry\-run feat/old\-branch
Preview removal without making changes.
.TP
reproctl wt attach
Pick a worktree interactively.
.TP
reproctl wt create \-i REP\-123
Create a worktree from a Linear issue.
.TP
reproctl worktree prune \-\-dry\-run
Preview which worktrees would be pruned.
